Subject: tools/power/x86/intel-speed-select: Fix link creation race in Makefile
From: Thomas Renninger <trenn@suse.de>
Patch-mainline: never, temporary_kbuild_workaround
References: bsc#1279549

Two links to kernel headers are created in Makefile:
thermal.h and isst_if.h
One (isst_if.h) is cleaned up in clean: section leading to the race:
Link to header file is removed before the build finished.
As a workaround do not clean up any of the header files
until a proper mainline workaround is found.

Signed-off-by: Thomas Renninger <trenn@suse.de>

---
 tools/power/x86/intel-speed-select/Makefile |    3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/tools/power/x86/intel-speed-select/Makefile
+++ b/tools/power/x86/intel-speed-select/Makefile
@@ -52,7 +52,6 @@
 
 clean:
 	rm -f $(ALL_PROGRAMS)
-	rm -rf $(OUTPUT)include/linux/isst_if.h
 	find $(or $(OUTPUT),.) -name '*.o' -delete -o -name '\.*.d' -delete
 
 install: $(ALL_PROGRAMS)
